---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Case Studies — ArchLab AI"
  description="Real results from real architecture projects. See how firms are using ArchLab to cut drafting time and costs."
  keywords="architecture AI case studies, ArchLab results"
>
<section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-label">Case Studies</span>
      <h1>Pilot Results from Architecture Firms <span class="text-gradient">Using ArchLab</span></h1>
      <p>Real projects, real metrics, real results. See how architecture firms are using ArchLab to transform their workflows.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- C3D Case Study -->
  <section class="content-block">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="reveal" style="background:var(--bg-alt);border:1px solid var(--border-dark);border-radius:20px;padding:48px;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:20px;margin-bottom:32px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <img src="/assets/c3d-logo.webp" alt="C3D Architects" style="height:48px;width:auto;" loading="lazy">
          <div>
            <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;margin-bottom:4px;">C3D Architects</h2>
            <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.9rem;">Chicago, Illinois &bull; Commercial Architecture</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 style="color:var(--accent);font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.1em;margin-bottom:16px;">Project Overview</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:24px;">A 12,000 square foot commercial retrofit in downtown Chicago. C3D Architects was engaged to document existing conditions across three floors and produce as-built drawings for a full interior renovation. The building was constructed in the 1920s with no reliable existing drawings available.</p>

        <h3 style="color:var(--accent);font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.1em;margin-bottom:16px;">The Challenge</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:24px;">Traditional approach would require a two-person team spending two full days on site with laser measuring equipment, followed by two additional days of drafting in AutoCAD. Total estimated cost: $4,800 in labour, equipment, and travel. Timeline: one week from site visit to deliverable drawings.</p>

        <h3 style="color:var(--accent);font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.1em;margin-bottom:16px;">The ArchLab Approach</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:24px;">One architect visited the site with a smartphone. Over 90 minutes, they photographed every room from multiple angles. The photographs were uploaded to ArchLab, which extracted dimensions, identified structural elements, and generated a complete floor plan within 47 minutes of processing time.</p>

        <div class="metric-grid" style="margin-top:32px;margin-bottom:32px;">
          <div class="metric-card">
            <h3>2 days &rarr; 47 min</h3>
            <p>Drafting time reduction</p>
          </div>
          <div class="metric-card">
            <h3>$4,800 &rarr; $680</h3>
            <p>Total project cost</p>
          </div>
          <div class="metric-card">
            <h3>0</h3>
            <p>Required revisits</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 style="color:var(--accent);font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.1em;margin-bottom:16px;">Key Takeaways</h3>
        <ul style="margin-bottom:24px;">
          <li style="padding:6px 0 6px 28px;position:relative;"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:var(--success);font-weight:700;">&#10003;</span> 86% reduction in as-built documentation costs</li>
          <li style="padding:6px 0 6px 28px;position:relative;"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:var(--success);font-weight:700;">&#10003;</span> Zero dimension errors requiring site revisits</li>
          <li style="padding:6px 0 6px 28px;position:relative;"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:var(--success);font-weight:700;">&#10003;</span> DXF output opened directly in AutoCAD without modification</li>
          <li style="padding:6px 0 6px 28px;position:relative;"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:var(--success);font-weight:700;">&#10003;</span> Freed junior architect for 1.5 days of design work</li>
        </ul>

        <blockquote style="border-left:3px solid var(--accent);padding-left:20px;margin:24px 0;font-style:italic;color:var(--text-heading-dark);font-size:1.05rem;">
          &ldquo;We used ArchLab on a commercial retrofit in Chicago and cut our as-built drafting time from two days to under an hour. The accuracy was indistinguishable from our manual measurements.&rdquo;
        </blockquote>
        <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.9rem;">&mdash; Cristian Nicolaie, Principal, C3D Architects</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- More coming -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="final-cta reveal">
        <h2 class="section-title">Want to Be Our Next Case Study?</h2>
        <p class="section-sub">We are actively expanding our pilot programme. Join as a pilot partner and get early access to ArchLab at founding-member rates.</p>
        <div class="hero-buttons">
          <a href="/for-firms" class="btn btn-primary">Request a Firm Demo <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
          <a href="/waitlist" class="btn btn-ghost">Join the Waitlist</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
